.TH TINYAMBIENT 1 "November 2026" "tinyAmbient 1.0.5" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tinyambient \- white, pink, and brown noise from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tinyambient
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoption\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tinyAmbient
generates white, pink, and brown noise and plays it through the audio stack the
desktop already runs. It opens no network connection and needs no runtime beyond
the C library and the system audio server.
.PP
The first invocation starts a small background process; every later invocation
forwards its command to that process. A session therefore survives between
terminals and shells. One daemon runs per user session: a second start forwards
instead of failing.
.PP
Commands may be written with or without a leading
.BR \-\- :
.B tinyambient noise brown
and
.B tinyambient \-\-noise brown
do the same thing.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B play
Start or resume playback.
.TP
.B pause
Pause playback and keep the daemon alive.
.TP
.B toggle
Switch between playing and paused.
.TP
.BI "noise " type
Select
.BR white ,
.BR pink ,
or
.BR brown .
The change crossfades over
.IR fade_ms .
.TP
.BI "volume " level
Set the volume, 0 to 100.
.TP
.BI "stop-after " "minutes|off"
Stop playback after
.I minutes
(1 to 10080), fading out over 20 seconds.
.B off
cancels a timer that is already running.
.TP
.B status
Print the current state as six lines of
.IR key = value .
.TP
.B quit
Stop the background process.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-noise " type
Same as the
.B noise
command.
.TP
.BI "\-\-volume " level
Same as the
.B volume
command.
.TP
.BI "\-\-stop-after " "minutes|off"
Same as the
.B stop-after
command.
.TP
.B \-\-mono
Generate one channel and send it to both ears.
.TP
.B \-\-stereo
Use independent generators per channel. This is the default.
.TP
.B \-\-portable
Read and write
.I config.ini
next to the executable instead of the per-user configuration directory.
.TP
.B \-\-foreground
Keep the daemon attached to the terminal and log lifecycle events to standard
error. The process does not detach.
.TP
.BI "\-\-render " file
Write noise to
.I file
instead of playing it. A
.B .wav
extension adds a WAV header; any other extension writes raw 32-bit float
samples. The render defaults are
.BR white ,
volume 100, 10 seconds, seed 1, and stereo.
.TP
.BI "\-\-seconds " n
Length of the render, 1 to 3600 seconds.
.TP
.BI "\-\-seed " n
Seed for the render. The same seed and arguments always produce the same file.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the state without starting a daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH STATUS
.B \-\-status
prints exactly six lines:
.PP
.nf
version=1.0.5
playing=1
noise=pink
volume=20
mono=0
stop_after=off
.fi
.PP
.B playing
is 1 while audio runs.
.B mono
is 1 when one channel is duplicated to both ears.
.B stop_after
is either
.B off
or the number of seconds left. The format is stable and intended for scripts.
.PP
With no daemon running,
.B \-\-status
reads the configuration and reports
.B playing=0
and
.BR stop_after=off ,
without starting one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tinyambient/config.ini
Per-user configuration on Linux, falling back to
.IR ~/.config/tinyambient/config.ini .
The file is small INI text; unknown keys and comments survive a rewrite.
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\\tinyAmbient\\config.ini
Per-user configuration on Windows.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/tinyambient.sock
The daemon's Unix socket on Linux, mode 0600. Without
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
the socket lives in a 0700 per-user directory under
.B TMPDIR
or
.IR /tmp .
.TP
.I %LOCALAPPDATA%\\tinyAmbient\\daemon\\tinyambient.exe
The copy of the binary the Windows daemon runs from. It lives outside the
installed directory so a package manager can replace the installed binary while
noise plays.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TINYAMBIENT_AUDIO
Set to
.B null
to use the null audio backend. Intended for the test suite and for machines
without a sound card.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure: no audio device, or the configuration could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.TP
.B 3
IPC failure: another daemon owns the single-instance address, or a command
could not be delivered.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tinyambient \-\-noise pink
tinyambient \-\-volume 35
tinyambient \-\-stop-after 90
tinyambient \-\-status
tinyambient \-\-quit
tinyambient \-\-render noise.wav \-\-noise brown \-\-seconds 30 \-\-seed 42
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/joaopmatos/tinyAmbient
